            "type": "output_text",
            "text": "**The latest major model release from xAI is Grok 4.6**, which launched on August 12, 2026.[[1]](https://tesorb.com/command/xai/)\n\n### Key details on Grok 4.6:\n- It focuses on improvements for long-running agents, interactive/visual work, coding, knowledge work, and ambitious projects.\n- It features a 500,000-token context window.\n- On the Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index, it scored approximately 60.92–61, nearly tying OpenAI’s GPT-5.6 Sol Max (60.93).[[1]](https://tesorb.com/command/xai/)\n- API pricing is listed around $2 per million input tokens and $6 per million output tokens.\n- It has been rolled out across platforms including GitHub Copilot (August 14), Amazon Bedrock, Microsoft Foundry, Google Vertex AI / Gemini Enterprise Agent Platform, and others in mid-to-late August 2026.[[2]](https://r.jina.ai/https:/x.ai/blog)\n\n### Upcoming: Grok 4.7\nOn September 2, 2026, Elon Musk announced that **Grok 4.7** is expected in about 10 days (around September 12, 2026).[[3]](https://cryptorank.io/news/feed/db1bc-grok-4-7-release-spacex-data)\n- It will scale up to **2.1 trillion parameters** (from 1.5T in 4.6).\n- Training incorporates unique SpaceX data for superior real-world engineering performance.\n- Musk claims it will “exceed all current models,” though he notes Anthropic may release improvements soon.\n- It is described as slightly slower but more token-efficient.\n\n### Other recent updates (not core model releases)\n- Grok Bot (agentic features) and Imagine (image/video generation) updates in July–August 2026.\n- Various platform integrations and Grok Build / voice improvements.\n\nFor the absolute latest official information, check [x.ai/blog](https://x.ai/blog) or [x.ai/news](https://x.ai/news), as releases happen frequently. The information above is based on announcements as of early September 2026.",
